Idamas.wikitext:
{{BloodAngelsPortal}}
'''Idamas''' was the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Blood Angels]]' [[99th Company (Blood Angels Legion)|99th Company]] during the [[Horus Heresy]] and he took part in the [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
However the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] was captured by [[Horus]]'s hordes during the [[Siege of Terra|Siege]] and was mutilated afterwards. In the last days of the invasion, Idamas would be among the captured prisoners that the [[Traitor]]s brought before the defenders of the [[Imperial_Palace#Inner_Palace|inner]] [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Delphic Battlement]]. This led directly to the [[Emperor]]'s domain within the [[Sanctum Imperialis]] and Horus wanted an ambassador sent to relay a message to the Imperials holding the Battlement. The [[Legio Mordaxis]]' [[Daughter of Torment]] was sent forth to do so and presented an offer to accept also present an insult to the [[Blood Angels]]' [[Primarch]] [[Sanguinus]], who had command of the Battlement. This insult was Idamas himself, who was fatally wounded by having 7 spears driven into him, in order to pin the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] to one of the Daughter's massive claws.{{Fn|1}} 

As it neared the [[Delphic Battlement|Battlement]], Idamas was finally seen by the [[Imperial]]s and his fellow [[Blood Angel]] [[Zephon (Blood Angels)|Zephon]] sought to rescue him. [[Sanguinius]] stopped Zephon, however, as the [[Primarch]] did not believe it was possible to save the captured [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], while the Daughter was still far from the Battlement. As more Imperials saw Idamas' mutilated form, they all began yelling their outrage at his treatment. This led the Daughter of Torment to complete [[Horus]]' insult to Sanguinus, by slowly crushing the impaled Captain to death in front of the Primarch. However before it could do so, Sanguinus ordered the nearby [[Skitarii]] [[Transacta-7Y1]] to kill Idamas. Despite the distance, Transacta made the shot and Idamas died right before his body was crushed by the Daughter of Torment.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
