Igmus Lothar.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
'''Igmus Lothar''' is a [[Traitor Commissar]] of the [[Styxx 777th Warwolves]], [[Traitor Guard]] [[Regiment]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
Like all of the [[Styxx 777th]], Lothar was once loyal to the [[Imperium]]{{Fn|1b}}, until they were sent to reinforce the [[Imperial]] world [[Moroch (Frontier World)|Moroch]] in [[M42]]. This was as the [[Imperium]] was [[Sanctus Wall|preparing]] for [[Abaddon the Despoiler]]'s hordes, as they [[Nachmund Rift War|bore down]] upon Moroch and the other worlds of the [[Gorandahl Sub-sector]]. The [[Black Legion]] became aware of this, however, and its [[Sorcerers]] determined which [[Regiments]] would be sent to reinforce the [[Sub-sector]]. This information was then given to the [[Alpha Legion]], whose [[Human]] agents infiltrated the targeted Regiments and began corrupting them to serve the Black Legion. The Styxx and other Regiments being sent to Moroch were infiltrated and successfully rotted from the inside out.{{Fn|1a}} 

Though Lothar had been a staunch [[Commissar]], his inherent lust for cruelty won over his [[Imperial Cult|faith]] and he joined the [[Styxx 777th]] in their [[Heresy]]{{Fn|1b}}. When [[Moroch (Frontier World)|Moroch]]'s reinforcements finally reached the world, they had all been fully corrupted by the [[Alpha Legion]] and were now loyal to the [[Black Legion]]{{Fn|1a}}. Lothar himself had risen in the Styxx 777th's ranks and became the most zealous of [[Traitor General (Traitor Guard)|Traitor General]] [[Seriadne Hekht]]'s [[Traitor Lieutenant]]s. He was also given a [[Chaos Ogryn]], named [[Drudge (Chaos Ogryn)|Drudge]], who served as his bodyguard and was also made Hekht's chief enforcer, which gave Lothar ample opportunity to vent his sadistic urges{{Fn|1b}}. It was days after arriving on Moroch, that the Traitor Guard revealed their treachery and began their attack to overthrow the Imperium's rule on the world. This would greatly aid the Black Legion, when its hordes [[Nachmund Rift War|invaded]] the [[Gorandahl Sub-sector]] and the Traitor Guard soon surrounded Moroch's capital '''Magnificentia'''{{Fn|1a}}. However a single [[Phobos Strike Team]], led by [[Vanguard Infiltrator#Types of Vanguard Infiltrators|Infiltrator Sergeant]] [[Justarian]], was sent to aid the besieged world. The [[Vanguard Space Marine]]s then began attacking the world's outposts, that were held by the Traitor Guard. The attacks soon forced the [[Regiment]]'s [[Traitor General (Traitor Guard)|Traitor Generals]] to respond, by sending [[Blooded Kill Team]]s to wipe out Justarian's Strike Team. These were led by their Lieutenants and General Hekht selected Lothar to lead a Kill Team, due to his zealously and, she hoped, loyalty to her. The [[Traitor Commissar]] would call it [[Lothar's Jackals]], but he did not lead them in immediately hunting down and attacking the Vanguard Marines. Instead he had the Jackals secretly watch Justarian's Strike Team, as they carried out their attacks on the outposts and easily dealt with the Blooded Kill Teams that found them.{{Fn|1b}} 

The Jackals bade their time, until Lothar was sure their attack would gain him glory and renown from the [[Chaos Gods]], instead of death{{Fn|1b}}. That moment came when the [[Phobos Strike Team]], attacked '''Outpost Furia-Epsil VII''' and were engaged in battle with its [[Traitor Guard]] garrison. Justarian had brought half his Strike Team for the attack and they were well within the Outpost, when Lothar's Jackals moved to launch their ambush against them{{Fn|1c}}. Though one of the Vanguard's spotted the Blooded Kill Team and attacked before they could get into position, the Jackals outnumbered the Strike Team and were prepared to fight the Strike Team. In the fierce battle that followed, Justarian and the Vanguards eventually gained the upper hand and forced Lothar to order his Blooded Kill Team to retreat. Though the [[Traitor Commissar]] and some of his Jackals managed to escape, the Strike Team had killed many of its members. However the Blooded Kill Team's ferocity had left several Vanguards laying dead in the Outpost as well. This was a dire blow to Justarian's Phobos Strike Team, as while Lothar's Jackals could easily find replacements for their losses, it was impossible for the Vanguards to do the same. The triumphant Traitor Commissar then willed [[Khorne|Ka'rn]] that the next time the Jackals attacked the Vanguards, they would be able to kill them all.{{Fn|1d}}

