Ihohet.wikitext:
{{AdeptusCustodesPortal}}
'''Ihohet''' was a [[Custodian]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]] and the [[Battle for Terra]].{{Fn|1b}} 
==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Mortis (Novel)}}
In the aftermath of the [[Battle for Terra|invasion]]'s [[Solar War]], Ihohet and two other [[Custodian]]s were aboard the [[Emperor]]'s command carrier [[Imperator Somnium]], as it joined other surviving [[Imperial]] warships that were under [[Admiral]] [[Niora Su-Kassen]]'s command. When a [[Dark Angels]] strike force led by [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]]-[[Paladin (Dark Angels)|Paladin]] [[Corswain]] later arrived in the [[Solar System]], the survivors rejoiced as they thought the might of the [[Primarch]]s [[Lion El'Jonson]] and [[Roboute Guilliman]] would soon aid them. However the Imperial fleet was disappointed to learn that Corswain's strike force was alone and he had thought his Primarch was already in the [[System]]. Shortly afterwards, the light of the [[Astronomican]] went out and if it was not relit, then there was no hope that the two Primarchs would be able to arrive to aid the Imperium. Corswain took it upon himself to lead his Dark Angels to Terra in order to relight the Astronomican, but they would need the aid of the Imperial fleet to do it. Terra was swarming with the warships of the traitorous [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]], and his small fleet, led by his flagship [[Wrath's Descent]], would not survive to reach the Throneworld's orbit. He brought his plan to Su-Kassen, but she was unwilling to send the entire Imperial fleet on a journey it would not return from, as they would be needed to aid the Primarchs when they arrived. A task that was given to her, by the Primarch [[Dorn]] himself. Su-Kassen instead{{Fn|1a}}, brought Corswain to Ihohet and the Dark Angel explained his plan to the Custodian. After hearing it, Ihohet agreed to lead the [[Imperator Somnium]] to Terra, where it would cut through the Warmaster's fleet. Its great size, would allow Corswain's fleet to hide in its shadow and its armor would ensure they reached Terra's orbit. All knew though, that this would be a final voyage for all the warships involved.{{Fn|1b}} 

After their ships were emptied of all but the most essential personnel, the [[Imperator Somnium]] and [[Dark Angels]]' fleet raced towards [[Terra]]. The [[Emperor]]'s command carrier soon came under fire from the [[Horus|Warmaster]]'s fleet, but it was able to reach the Throneworld's orbit. As [[Corswain]]'s fleet then prepared to launch the Dark Angels towards the [[Forbidden Fortress]], which contained the [[Astronomican]], Ihohet contacted the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]]-[[Paladin (Dark Angels)|Paladin]]. Even as the Imperator Somnium began to burn around him, Ihohet calmly informed Corswain that his two fellow [[Custodian]]s would be joining the Dark Angels as they stormed the Forbidden Fortress. The Custodian went on to state, however, that he would be remaining aboard the Imperator Somnium, until the end. Corswain wished honor upon Ihohet, who then ended the communication and shortly afterwards the Dark Angels and Custodians successfully launched from their ships. The Warmaster's fleet then focused their fire on the Dark Angels' fleet as well, which sent them aflame and adrift alongside the Imperator Somnium. By then the Emperor's command carrier had been critically damaged and it collided with Corswain's flagship, the [[Wrath's Descent]]. This then caused the Imperator Somnium to explode in a massive wave of golden fire, which consumed all the ships that were near it.{{Fn|1b}}

==Sources==
