Illiyan Nastase.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
{{Otheruses|USE=1st Edition Ultramarines Chief Librarian|OTHERUSE=Eldar Farseer|OTHERPAGE=Illiyanne Natasé}}

{{QuoteBox|quote='''<nowiki>[</nowiki>[[Keorn Asata|Asata]]<nowiki>]</nowiki> was not surprised to see the elegant form of Astropath Illiyan Nastase staring out sightlessly from the edge of the ramparts. The half-human psyker never failed to unnerve him. As he approached, the shrill voice of the bastard pierced the hot evening air. 'Captain Keorn Asata', he announced, without turning his head, 'your footfalls are as distinctive as an [[Ambull]] dancing upon a tile roof.''''{{Fn|1a}}}}
'''Illiyan Nastase''' is a half-[[Eldar]], half-[[Human]] [[Imperial]] [[Astropath]], who was the [[Chief Librarian]] of the [[Ultramarines]] in late [[M41]]. Before this, Nastase had been a [[Consul]] helping to run the advisory [[Senate]] to the [[Master of the Adeptus Astra Telepathica|Master]] of the [[Adeptus Astra Telepathica]], and had assignments with the [[Imperial Fleet]] and [[Dark Angels]] Chapter.{{Fn|1b}}

==History==
[[Image:NataseRT.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Illiyan Nastase{{Fn|1b}}]]
[[Image:Nastase Imprisoned.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Illiyan Nastase imprisoned by [[Trazyn the Infinite]] in a non-canon satirical comic{{Fn|6}}]]

Nastase was born on [[Badab]] in [[Ultima Segmentum]] following the expulsion of the [[Chaos|traitor]] [[planetary governor]] [[Lufgt Huron]] in 912.[[M41]]. He was a bastard, with a [[Human]] mother and an unknown [[Eldar]] [[mercenary]] father. He was gene-tested at birth in accordance with [[Imperial Law]], and was subsequently taken into Imperial custody.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

He was reared in the government compound by the [[Imperial Mission]] which had taken over running Badab after the [[Badab War]]. Nastase was considered a potential [[psyker|psychic]], and undertook the journey to [[Terra]] in 924.[[M41]] along with other potential psychics. On Terra, further tests led to him undergoing the [[Soul Binding]] ritual in 925.[[M41]], which scarred and blinded him. From that point, Nastase was recruited into the [[Administratum]] as an [[Imperial]] [[Astropath]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

Nastase attained the ranks of [[Astropath Secundus|Secundus]], [[Prefect]] and eventually rose to become [[Consul]] for four years, helping to run the [[Adeptus Terra]]'s advisory [[Senate]] to the [[Master of the Adeptus Astra Telepathica|Master]] of the [[Adeptus Astra Telepathica]]. After this he undertook four years service with the [[Imperial Fleet|Fleet]], and a further two years with the [[Dark Angels]] Chapter.{{Fn|1b}}

Following this, he was appointed as chief of the [[Macragge]] [[interstellar communications link]] under the jurisdiction of the [[Ultramarines]] in 965.[[M41]]. By 987.[[M41]], Nastase had become the Ultramarines [[Chief Librarian]], with his own unique Ultramarines badge. As an [[Astropath]], Nastase remained a member of the [[Adeptus Astra Telepathica]] during his posting, ultimately answering to the [[Adeptus Terra]], and was not a [[Space Marine]] despite holding office within the Chapter, and being given [[Power Armour]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|1d}}

Nastase was stationed at an [[Ultramarines]] fortress, along with [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Keorn Asata]], who he talked to countless times, and the sound of whose footsteps he came to recognise. Despite this, his presence was still always unnerving to Asata, who was highly suspicious of [[psykers]], and even considering killing him and spat venomously before speaking to him.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1e}}

During an [[Ambull]] hunt to test new Ultramarines recruits, Nastase was positioned on the fortress' uppermost battlements, staring sightlessly from the edge of the ramparts. He was able to faintly pick up the recruits [[Telepathy|telepathically]], and thought that they must have taken more casualties than anticipated due to how faint their signal was. He heard [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Keorn Asata|Asata]] approach, talked with him about this, and patiently listened to the anecdote he had heard many times before of Asata's initiation.{{Fn|1a}}

==Biology==
[[Image:IlliyanNastaseBadge.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Illiyan Nastase's Ultramarines Badge{{Fn|1d}}]]
As half-[[Eldar]], half-[[Human]], Nastase had an elegant form, a shrill voice, and a strangely delicate face with a long aristocratic nose, tight but large lips, and characteristically sharp ears. As an Astropath, Nastase was blind, with empty eyes hidden by dark [[plasflex]] hemispheres almost concealing the puckered scar tissue around his eye sockets.{{Fn|1a}} By 987.[[M41]], Nastase was seventy-six years old, but thanks to his [[Eldar]] ancestry showed little signs of aging.{{Fn|1b}}

===Psychic Abilities===
Nastase had [[Psyker|psychic]] abilities: an innate Psychic Sense and Psychic Awareness, [[Astrotelepathy]], the abilities to become a Psychic Beacon, to Resist Psychic Attacks, to Sense Presences (including being able to detect a unit of new recruits from a distance),{{Fn|1a}} and detect Warp Space Trails. He could cure injuries, and had some Immunity from Poison. He was [[Telekinesis|Telekinetic]], and offensively could Steal Minds, and use [[Mental Bolt]]s.{{Fn|1b}}

==Equipment==
Nastase wore [[Mark VI]] [[Power Armour]], with a unique shoulder pad badge. In combat he carried a [[Force Sword]] and [[Laspistol]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1d}}

==Quotes==
* "Captain [[Keorn Asata]], your footfalls are as distinctive as an [[Ambull]] dancing upon a tile roof."{{Fn|1a}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
* The name Illiyan Nastase may have been inspired by 1970s Romanian tennis player [[wikipedia:Ilie Năstase|Ilie Năstase]].
* In-universe, Illiyan is an [[Eldar]] name, used for example by [[Illiyan (House of Arienal)|Illiyan]] the grandfather of [[Iyanna Arienal]].{{Fn|2}}
*In a satirical comic released by Warhammer Community Nastase was seen among the [[Ultramarines]] that were captured by the [[Necron Overlord]] [[Trazyn the Infinite]]. He was now among the Overlord's possessions, that are put on display on the [[Tomb World]] [[Solemnace]].{{Fn|6}} 
===Conflicting sources===
* [[Illiyanne Natasé]] was introduced in the 2021 novel [[The Gate of Bones (Novel)|The Gate of Bones]], as a [[Farseer]] of [[Ulthwe]] sent to warn [[Ultramarines]] [[Primarch]] [[Roboute Guilliman]].{{Fn|3}}
* Apart from this, Illiyan Nastase has only been mentioned once{{Fn|6}} since the 1st Edition, with [[Varro Tigurius]] said to be the [[Ultramarines]] [[Chief Librarian]] since at least 848.[[M41]], remaining in post after the return of [[Roboute Guilliman]] around 999.[[M41]].{{Fn|4}}{{Fn|5}}

