Imurah.wikitext:
{{ThousandSonsPortal}}
[[File:Imurah.jpeg|thumb|Imurah{{Fn|2}}]]
'''Imurah''' was a [[Chaos Lord|Sorcerer Lord]] of the [[Thousand Sons]] [[Chaos Space Marine|Chaos]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] who led an invasion on [[Avarax]] and faced off against [[Demetrian Titus|Lieutenant Titus]] and the [[Ultramarines]].{{Fn|1}}

200 years before the events of [[Space Marine II]], Imurah battled [[Marneus Calgar]] and was cast into the [[warp]] to face the wrath of [[Tzeentch]] for a time.{{Fn|1c}} He later reappeared and intended to acquire the [[Project Aurora|Aurora device]] on Avarax. To that end, Imurah manipulated the [[Mechanicum]] [[Tech-Priest]] [[Morias Leuze]] into completing his work.{{Fn|1a}} After initially feigning weakness to the Aurora device, Imurah waited until Leuze had completed his preparations before killing the Tech-Priest and activating the array.{{Fn|1b}} Imurah opened a large [[Warp Portal]] with the Aurora Device from which an allied [[Lord of Change]] emerged and battled the Ultramarines now led by [[Marneus Calgar]].{{Fn|1c}}

After Titus and his squad were successful in realigning the Aurora and weakening the Warp rift, Imurah and the Lord of Change fled back into the warp with the device, but were pursued by [[Calgar]], [[Titus]], [[Gadriel]], and [[Chairon]]. While in battle, Imurah revealed that he intended to use the Aurora device to amplify his warp powers and gain "divine knowledge", but during the ritual Titus realigned it. The subsequent implosion caused Imurah's body to disintegrate.{{Fn|1c}}

