Incedia Chorda.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
[[Image:incedia chorda.jpg|thumb|right|350px|Portrait of Incedia Chorda{{Fn|2}}]]
'''Incedia Chorda''' was an heir of the [[Rogue Trader]] [[House Chorda]]. As of [[M42]] she has overtaken the House's [[Warrant of Trade]] and became active in the [[Koronus Expanse]], destroying piracy and rebellion in the [[Sector]].{{Fn|1}}

==The Drusian Rogue Trader==
Her predecessor [[Aspyce Chorda]] kept her in a [[Cryo Vault]] along with much of her family to avoid any potential takeover. Saint Drusus missionaries discovered this secret repository but only when all of her kin had already died due to equipment failures and she suffered physiological damage she never recovered from. For 3 years, she was paralyzed, blind with only the prayers of the priests to keep from losing her mind. She vowed to pursue Aspyce and others like her to her last breath.{{Fn|1}}

Unlike her predecessor [[Aspyce Chorda]], Incedia is highly devout to the [[Imperial Cult]], having the backing of the [[Drusians]] on [[Footfall]]. [[Hieronymus Doloroso]] considers himself her personal confessor and guide. With Aspyce missing - having disappeared into the Koronus Expanse - and Incedia as the sole member left of the House, she has taken control as the House's Lord Captain.{{Fn|1}}

