Indrick Boreale.wikitext:
{{BloodRavensPortal}}
[[Brother-Captain]] '''Indrick Boreale''' of the [[Blood Ravens]] was a student of the famed [[Space Marine Captain|Brother-Captain]] [[Gabriel Angelos]] and [[Space Marine Commander|Force Commander]] in the [[Kaurava]] Conflict.{{Fn|1}}

== History ==
[[Image:Indrick Boreale.jpg|thumb|right|Captain Indrick Boreale]]
Boreale was forced to battle fellow [[Imperial]] forces  of the [[Sisters of Battle]] and the [[252nd Conservator Regiment]] of the [[Imperial Guard]] due to conflicting orders and interests.{{Fn|1}}

When on the defence he favoured a tactic known as [[Steel Rain]], which made extensive use of [[drop pods]] to overwhelm and pressure the enemy. Because of this, he made little use of static defenses such as turrets, preferring to rely on speed and mobility to achieve victory.{{Fn|1}}

Boreale was the captain chosen to lead five Blood Ravens companies, comprising fully half of the chapter, in the Kaurava campaign. The campaign ended in disaster, as Boreale and his forces were wiped out in a crushing blow to the chapter. This defeat left the Blood Ravens drastically low on manpower in the days leading into the [[First Aurelian Crusade]], and is looked upon with shame by many in the chapter.{{Fn|2}}{{Fn|3}}

== Wargear ==
Boreale starts the campaign with a standard issue [[bolt pistol]] and [[chainsword]] but also has access to the [[master-crafted]] [[power mace]] ''[[Rogal's Fist]]'' and a [[Daemonhammer]].{{Fn|1}}

He is able to upgrade his long range arsenal to a [[plasma pistol]] and to a [[meltagun]]. His basic [[Power armour]] can also be upgraded to [[Artificer Armour]] and have "Errant"-pattern [[greaves]] installed on his legs to increase his movement speed and health. He can also receive the prestigious [[Iron Halo]], the [[Blood Ravens]] [[Chapter Banner]], and a back mounted [[teleport]] device.{{Fn|1}}

