Inigo Ravellon.wikitext:
{{EcclesiarchyPortal}}
'''Inigo Ravellon''' is an [[Ecclesiarchy]] [[Bishop-Praetor]] of [[Varentis II]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was present on the world, when a series of insurrections began in its city-states. Now matter how many were put down by [[Varentis II]]'s [[Adeptus Arbites]] or [[PDF]], more sprang up elsewhere. The world's [[Ecclesiarchy]], soon discovered the insurrections' [[Heretical]] leanings, but by then the ruling [[Planetary Governor|Heptarchy]] grip on Varentis had greatly deteriorated. This led Ravellon and the senior members of the Ecclesiarchy, to decide to call upon the [[Order of Our Martyred Lady]] for aid. They knew the Heptarchy was now no longer able to handle, what was obviously becoming a [[Chaos Cult]] uprising. A fleet, led by [[Canoness Preceptor]] [[Moirelle]], was sent to restore the [[Imperium]]'s rule of [[Varentis II]], but the tides of the [[Warp]] worked against it. When they finally arrived, the fleet discovered Varentis was fully in the grips of [[Heretics]]. By then, Ravellon had become one of the few Ecclesiarchy survivors in the capital city-state of '''Varent-har'''.{{Fn|1}}   

For several months, before the fleet arrived, he waged a guerrilla war against the [[Heretic]]s at the head of a civilian militia. When [[Moirelle]]'s forces invaded the world, Ravellon and the militia were hidden in the crypts of the desecrated '''Cathedrum Mirabilis''', which was held by Heretics. The [[Canoness Preceptor]] later fought to cleanse the Cathedrum, which led Ravellon to go to their aid with the militia after he heard the [[Adeptus Sororitas]]' battle psalms. Their sudden appearance gave the Sororitas time to recover, but many of the militia were killed before they could reach the Heretics. However between their two forces, the Sororitas and militia completely cleansed the Cathedrum. Moirelle's forces would then go on to reclaim Varentis II's city-states and restore the [[Imperium]]'s rule on the world. Afterwards, the ruling members of the [[Planetary Governor|Heptarchy]] suffered greatly at [[Moirelle]]'s hands. For failing to defend [[Varentis II]], the bodies of each of Heptarchy's dynasties were taken and made to line the major transit ways of the city-states in [[Stasis]]-sealed moments of agony. Purges also continued on the world for more than a year, under the oversight of Ravellon. Finally by [[Ecclesiarchal]] decree, and approved by the [[High Lords]], Ravellon brought Varentis II under the direct rule of the Ecclesiarchy. It was then rededicated as a [[Shrine World]], in the name of those who had fallen in the world's defense.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
