Isa (Noble).wikitext:
{{ImperialKnightsPortal}}
'''Isa''' is a [[Noble]] of the [[Imperial Knight]] [[Knight House|House]] [[House Dreyrskilde|Dreyrskilde]], who is undergoing her [[Ritual of Becoming]].{{Fn|1}}

She was escorted to [[House Dreyrskilde]]'s [[Chamber of Echoes]] by her father, but he remained outside the Chamber. The young [[Noble]] was then able to glimpse her father's stern but hopeful face, before its doors were closed. The [[Sacristan]] [[Herrolf]], would soon oversee Isa's insertion into a [[Throne Mechanicum]] and with that, her [[Ritual of Becoming]] began. If the Noble succeeded, she would become a [[Knight]] and would be able to claim Dreyrskilde as her last name. When Isa then opened her eyes, she found herself within a dark moonlit forest, but the Noble could not remember who she was. The loss was only temporary though, and her memories quickly returned to her. This included the preparations Dreyrskilde's precepts gave Isa to complete the Ritual, along with her combat training and lessons about the House's history.{{Fn|1}} 

Thanks to all of this, she was able to find the ruins of a stronghold, which was home to a large and dangerous beast. Though Isa's combat skills with a sword allowed her to wound the creature, it was able to rapidly heal the damage. The [[Noble]] also had to content with the unseen spirits of the [[Throne Mechanicum]]'s previous [[Knight]]s, who prodded and jabbed Isa, as they admonished or encouraged her. All of this would have allowed the beast to kill the Noble, had she not then recognized a shield that was embedded into the creature's shoulder. It was displayed in [[House Dreyrskilde]]'s oldest monument, which showed its founder slaying a figure representing dishonor. The shield was carried by the defeated foe and this led Isa to conclude that she had to destroy it. The Noble did so, with a might swing of her sword and once the shield was shattered, the beast died immediately. However this was just part of her [[Ritual of Becoming]] and Isa readied herself, as chimeric shadows then bore down on her.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Imperial Knights (10th Edition)]], pgs. 48-49

