Isaac Shiller.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Isaac Shiller''' was a [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] in the [[Royal Volpone 50th]], during the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
He was a 6th generation [[Royal Volpone 50th|Royal]], who came from a long line of high-ranking military men. While this led Shiller to have lofty aspirations about his future, he was marred by his ill-temper and bad habits. This included excessive drinking while on duty and being abusive to the Regiment's [[Mil-serve]] servants. Due to their lowborn status, however, Shiller refused to call them that and used the derogatory slur '''Deg''' instead. During the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]], the 50th were among its forces that fought the [[Blood Pact]] on [[Gnostes]]. There, some of its [[Imperial Guard Company|Companies]] were among the [[Regiments]] that [[General]] [[Voke (General)|Voke]] commanded, as he defended the city of '''Lodden'''. As the Blood Pact attacked the city, the Royals suffered causalities, including amongst their officer class. Shiller and [[Lieutenant (Imperial Guard)|Lieutenant]] [[Armand Culcis]], were eventually among the only three left and were then under the command of [[Major]] [[Vasquez Regara]]. As they fought to defend the city, the Captain would continue his bad habits. This forced Major Regara to have to remind Shiller to maintain a decorum fitting of a Royal Volpone officer. Disaster later struck, during the battle as the [[Blood Pact]] advanced upon Lodden'. General Voke's tactics to fight the [[Heretics]] backfired, when his overextended battle line was overrun. This led the General to give the order for his Regiments to retreat and abandon the city. Shiller and the 50th then joined the other surviving [[Guardsmen]], as they tried to escape before the Blood Pact overwhelmed them.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Volpone Glory (Novel)]], Chapter 1
