Ishmayn.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinePortal}}
'''Ishmayn''' is a [[Novamarines]] [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], who has served his [[Chapter]] for three centuries. He currently commands the Novamarines' [[Strike Force Ishmayn]], which is part of [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Secundus]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
During the [[Nachmund Rift War]], his [[Novamarines]] were among the [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Secundus|Secundus]]' forces that defended the [[Sanctus Wall]] world [[Catagyl]] from a [[Chaos]] invasion. As the battle raged there, several [[Geskan]] [[Astra Militarum]] [[Regiments]] defending the '''Mountain-plex Ajax''' were destroyed by a horde of [[Chaos Cultists]] and a few [[Alpha Legion]] [[Chaos Space Marines]] that were aiding them. In order to ensure Ajax did not fall, [[Strike Force Ishmayn]] was charged with protecting the Mountain-plex's entrance, until the [[Imperial Knights]] of [[House Gryphonne]] reached their position. Once they arrived, the two sides would then work together to destroy the Chaos forces. However before this could occur, they were attacked by the [[Black Legion]] [[Sorcerer]] known as the [[Thirteenth Curse|Fiend]].{{Fn|1}}  

[[Strike Force Ishmayn]] was then frozen in place by the [[Thirteenth Curse|Fiend]], as the powerful [[Sorcerer]] began tearing them all apart. [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] Ishmayn could only helplessly watch in agony, as his [[Novamarines]] began dying around him. Worse still, the Strike Force was unable to defend itself as the [[Chaos Cultists]] and [[Alpha Legion]] reached them. Though just as it appeared likely that the Novamarines would all die, thirty members of the [[Sisters of Silence]] suddenly appeared before them. Their target was the Fiend and the Sisters' [[Blank]] abilities broke the hold the [[Sorcerer]] had on the Strike Force. The Fiend was left helpless by the Sisters' presence and was decapitated by them, even as his acolytes attempted to aid him. This enraged the Cultists who began attacking the outnumbered Sisters in a frenzy. Though he was left heavily wounded by the Sorcerer's attack, Ishmayn rallied his surviving Novamarines to go to the aid of their saviors. While only half of Strike Force Ishmayn's members remained alive, the Captain was sure they would hold for the four minutes it would take for [[House Gryphonne]]'s [[Knights]] to reach their location. Once they did, the Imperials would unite to destroy the Chaos forces.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Adeptus Custodes (10th Edition)]], pgs. 30-33 - ''The Silent Sisterhood''

