Isk'ayn.wikitext:
{{SlaaneshPortal}}
'''Isk'ayn''' is a [[Slaanesh]] [[Keeper of Secrets]], who commands the [[Chaos God]]'s [[Legion of Avarice]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
In [[M42]], it was among the [[Daemons]] of [[Slaanesh]] who invaded the [[Imperial]] world [[Persiphon]]. This was after a civil war broke out between the world's six '''Halls of Excellence''', which competed against each other to be judged the best at training the world's highly rated [[Guardsmen]]. The need to achieve victory, later led each of the Halls' war clerics to appeal to [[Chaos|dark powers]] and caused [[Slaanesh]]'s Daemons to invade Persiphon. Isk'ayn and five other [[Keepers of Secrets|Keepers]] would join the attack and laid claim to the world. The influence of the Keepers of Secrets enveloped Persiphon and caused the veil between the [[warp]] and [[realspace]] to weaken further. As a result, nightmarish transformations had swept across the world and each Keeper ruled a unique realm, from the now corrupted Halls of Excellence. The citysprawl of [[Randa]] became the playground of Isk'ayn and its [[Legion of Avarice]]. These Daemons mocked, tempted and slayed the city's two billion inhabitants and garrison troops, as they became obsessed with seizing Randa's wealth for themselves and began falling upon each to do so. Though an [[Ultramarines]] strike force, led by [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Aurus (Captain)|Aurus]], has now come to Persiphon' aid, the [[Space Marines]] are heavily outnumbered by Slaanesh's Daemons and the world's corrupted population. This has led [[Inquisitor]] [[Rudran Luc]] to call upon the [[Grey Knights]] for aid in saving Persiphon.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Chaos Daemons (9th Edition)]], pgs. 26-27 - ''War Zone: Persiphon''

