Iskhandrian.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Iskhandrian''' was a [[General|Captain-General]] of the [[Atraxian Regiments]] active in the late 300's.[[M41]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
By '''397.[[M41]]''' Iskhandrian had developed a good war record, notably fighting against the [[ork]]s on a number of occasions. However, he also had a reputation for dogmatism. In addition, he tended to lay the blame for his own mistakes on his subordinates.{{Fn|1b}} He had [[Imperial Guard Commander|overall command]] of the [[Astra Militarum]] forces in the [[Kalidar War]].{{Fn|1a}}

At one point in the war, following a string of victories by Imperial forces against the orks of [[Waaagh! Gratzdakka]], Iskhandrian hosted a banquet aboard the [[Command Leviathan]] ''[[Magnificence (Leviathan)|Magnificence]]''.{{Fn|1a}} However, a [[Blood Axes]] warband used a sandstorm raging over [[Macaree's Tablelands|the plains]] to attack the ''Magnificence'' and the troops stationed nearby. The orks were repelled, but not before inflicting serious damage to the Leviathan and a number of the Militarum's tanks and killing several officers.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}} Afterwards, Iskhandrian had charges filed against [[Tulligen|a number]] [[Ostilek|of officers]] [[Gemael|for unacceptable inflexibility]] in the face of the ork attack.{{Fn|1b}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*The character's name may be based on ''Iskandar'' or ''Iskander'', Persian renderings of the name ''Alexander'' which were originally used to refer to [[Wikipedia:Alexander the Great|Alexander the Great]].
===Notes===
*At one point in the source, the character's name is given as '''Iskhandria'''.{{Fn|1a}} This is presumably an error.

