Itha Clathis.wikitext:
{{SonsOfHorusPortal}}
'''Itha Clathis''' was a member of the [[Sons of Horus]], who served in [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Azelas Baraxa]]'s [[2nd Company (Sons of Horus)|2nd Company]], near the end of the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
After the closing of the [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Eternity Gate (Imperial)|Eternity Gate]], Clathis was among [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]]' forces as they attacked any [[Imperials]] remaining within the [[Inner Palace]]. This included the Palace's '''Radium Gate''', which was held by the [[Imperial Fists]]. However as the [[Traitor]]s charged at the Gate's fortifications, the Fists launched a flanking attack that caught the Warmaster's hordes off-guard. Among the [[Loyalist]]s, was an Imperial Fist who wielded two [[power axe]]s, which he used to strike Clathis with a powerful blow. This launched the Sons of Horus' blood and bone fragments into the air and it is not known if Clathis survived the attack.{{Fn|1b}} 

This would gain the attention of the [[Traitor Legion|Legion]]'s [[First Captain]] [[Abaddon]], though, who thought that due to the [[Imperial Fists]]' fighting style and weapons, that it was [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Fafnir Rann]]. Abaddon sought to claim the Imperial Fist's life as a trophy and so charged at the rampaging [[Loyalist]], as he struck a glancing blow to the Sons of Horus [[Kaltos]]. It was as the Imperial Fist sought to strike down [[Tyro Gamex]], that Abaddon was finally able to reach the Loyalist and kill him. However after the First Captain removed the slain Imperial Fist's helmet, he realized it was not Rann, but some unknown member of the Loyalist Legion, that Abaddon did not recognize.{{Fn|1b}}

==Sources==
