Ivandar.wikitext:
{{ChaosKnightsPortal}}
'''Ivandar''' was a member of [[House Lucaris]] who piloted the [[Knight Tyrant]] [[Death of Hope (Chaos Knight)|Death of Hope]]. He was killed during the War on [[Turris]].{{Fn|1}}

===Overview===
Having survived since the [[Horus Heresy]], Ivandar had his life prolonged through unknown means, possibly arcane technology or [[Chaos]] [[Sorcery]] to survive more than ten thousand years before being defeated by the [[Imperial Knight|Loyalist]] [[Knight Warden]] ''Heartsbane'' of [[House Cadmus]]. He had nursed a millenia-long grudge against House Cadmus, in particular ''Heartsbane'' and its pilots, following a humiliating defeat to it in a tourney and the house's refusal to join the forces of [[Horus]]. This grudge led him to disregard reason and safety whenever ''Heartsbane'' took the field, ignoring all else in favour of claiming vengeance, though despite multiple attempts he never succeeded. This blind obsession contributed to his eventual demise, when ''Heartsbane'' and others within it's Lance were able to lure him into a trap and kill him once and for all.{{Fn|1}}

===Appearance and Personality===
Initially described as 'powerfully built' and 'balding', after thousands of years of corruption, he instead resembled a mutated mess of flesh and machine, well and truly fused with his corrupted [[Throne Mechanicum]], with his malice-filled eyes being described as one of the only human features he possessed.{{Fn|1}}

Prior to his ultimate corruption, he was quick to anger and hide-bound regarding tradition and tactics. By the end of his life he was utterly insane and filled with hatred and bloodlust, though he had also become more flexible and adopted some of the strategies and armaments of his foes.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}} [[Apex Predator (Short Story)]]
