Ix'thar'ganix.wikitext:
{{TzeentchPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Lord of Change]] of [[Tzeentch]], also known as the '''Slayer of Destinies'''.{{Fn|1}}

==History==
After the creation of the [[Grey Knights]] [[Chapter]], Ix'thar'ganix foresaw the role they would play in his downfall and the threat the Chapter may eventually pose to the [[Chaos Gods]]. Overcome with his own cunning, the Lord of Change began a plan that would take eight thousand years to come to fruition and seeded lesser Daemons on worlds all across the [[Imperium]], so that he might subtly manipulate future events.{{Fn|3}}

When [[Tzeentch]] had given the Daemon a glimpse of a young child born on the world of [[Omegath]] who would eventually become a powerful oracle, Ix'thar'ganix would crave the boy's power and used all of his magic to open a [[warp rift]], entering the [[Materium]] and leading a daemonic invasion of the world. Not knowing the exact location of the boy, for twenty days the forces of Ix'thar'ganix ravaged the planet, battling the world's [[Planetary Defense Forces]]. Eventually running across an old farm commune, the Lord of Change finally discovered his prize and stole the child's power of foresight. His daemonic legions vanished soon after.{{Fn|1}}

Ix'Thar'ganix appeared once more in the [[Plague of Madness]] of 941.[[M41]], manipulating the [[Great Unclean One]] [[Lurgon]] into battling the [[Grey Knights]].{{Fn|2}}

