Jaegar Silverclaw.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''Jaegar Silverclaw''' was the first [[Wolf Lord]] to command the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter]]'s [[Silverclaws]] [[Great Company]], until he was slain in battle. He was then succeeded as the Silverclaws' Wolf Lord by [[Kvalnir Silverclaw]], who chose not to change the Great Company's name.{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
The end of his reign as the [[Silverclaws]]' [[Wolf Lord]] came during the [[Space Wolves]]' [[Great Hunt|Fifth Great Hunt]], as they did battle with the [[Thousand Sons]]. At that time, Jaegar and the Silverclaws were taking part in their [[Chapter]]'s invasion of a world that was held by the [[Traitor Legion]], when its [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Magnus]] suddenly appeared from the [[Warp]]. Magnus then created a [[Warp Rift]] in front of Jaegar and his [[Wolf Guard]], just as the Wolf Lord been leading the [[Great Company]] to victory over the Thousand Sons. This ended in mere moments, though, when the forces of [[Tzeentch]] emerged from the Warp Rift and fell upon the Wolf Lord in overwhelming numbers. Though his Wolf Guard was beside him, Jaegar knew his death was at hand and ferociously fought like a cornered wolf, until he was finally slain. Magnus' trap nearly undid the Silverclaws then and there, as Jaegar's death and the sudden wave of new foes, caused the Great Company to begin retreating. It was only thanks to the quick thinking of the [[Long Fang]] [[Kvalnir Silverclaw]] that a disaster was avoided, as he managed to rally the Silverclaws to him. The Great Company then began to push Tzeentch's hordes back into the Warp Rift, which the Silverclaws' [[Rune Priest]]s successfully closed. The Great Company then regrouped to drive the Thousand Sons from the world.{{Fn|1b}}

In the aftermath of the battle, it was discovered that Jaegar's entire [[Wolf Guard]] died with him and this complicated the matter of choosing his successor. Normally it would be from their ranks that a new [[Wolf Lord]] was chosen, but this was no longer an option for the [[Silverclaws]], and so the [[Space Wolves]]' [[Great Wolf]], [[Logan Grimnar]], intervened on their behalf. He ultimately decided to bestow [[Kvalnir Silverclaw|Kvalnir]] with the the honor of succeeding Jaegr, due to the [[Long Fang]]'s leadership during the battle, which saved the Space Wolves from certain defeat. After becoming a Wolf Lord, Kvalnir decided against changing his [[Great Company]]'s [[Wolf Totem]] the '''Silverclaw'''. It was the Silverclaws he led to victory against [[Tzeentch]]'s hordes in the [[Great Hunt|Fifth Great Hunt]] and so the Silverclaws they would remain.{{Fn|1b}} Jaegar is still remembered though, as his saga is among those told by [[Rune Priest]]s before the [[Chapter]] undergoes a Great Hunt. Doing so inspires the Space Wolves to achieve the greatest heights of courage and heroism.{{Fn|2}} 
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
