Jaku Dihardis.wikitext:
{{AssassinorumPortal}}
'''Jaku Dihardis''' is an [[Imperial Assassin]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
While most are taken from [[Feral World]]s during infancy, Jaku is something of a rarity. He is from a [[Hive World]], and was recruited at the very late age of 14. The reasons for these breaks with normal practice were simple: the [[Officio Assassinorum]] required an operative who was at home on Hive Worlds, in order to remove troublesome [[Imperial Commander]]s. After eight years of intensive training, Jaku was returned to his [[Homeworld]] and then quickly eliminated its Commander. This allowed the [[Assassin]] to assume control of the Hive World, which he turned over to its new Imperial Commander after three months. Since then, Jaku has specialized in assassinations and impersonations on Hive Worlds, where his upbringing gives him a distinct advantage over other Assassins.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Warhammer 40,000 Chapter Approved - The Book of the Astronomican]], pg. 108 - ''Imperial Characters''
