Jangsai Khan.wikitext:
{{WhiteScarsPortal}}
'''Jangsai Khan''' was the [[Space Marine Captain|Khan]] of the [[White Scars]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]'s [[Brotherhood of the Iron Axe]], during the later years of the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
[[Image:Jangsai.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Jangsai Khan{{Fn|1a}}]]
He was born as '''Tuyo''' on the [[Imperial]] world [[Ar Rija]], which became a training site for [[Aspirant]]s who would serve the [[Loyalist]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legions]] after the [[Horus Heresy]] began. His parents despaired when Tuyo was selected and he held onto his last memory of them as he underwent his training. It was the last tether to his old life but, despite his determination, months of mental conditioning caused him to lose it. Because the Loyalist Legions were desperate for reinforcements, Tuyo and his fellow Aspirants underwent expedited suboptimal training. However, they were far from finished when Ar Rija was attacked by the [[Traitor]] forces of [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]]. Tuyo and the Aspirants were spirited away in order to complete their training as Ar Rija was invaded. As he was taken to safety, Tuyo's last [[Human]] attachment to his homeworld made him hope it was destroyed by the Traitors. He had had learned that Loyalist worlds suffered greatly at the Warmaster's hands.{{Fn|1a}} 

Afterwards his training would continue and would be eventually be completed on [[Terra]]. This was before the [[Siege of Terra]] began, but Tuyo knew it would be his first battle and his last if he died there. He was proud, though, as he was selected to become a member of the [[White Scars]], who were one of the three Loyalist Legions defending Terra. Tuyo and his other fellow White Scar Aspirants were then initiated into the Legion by [[Ganzorig Noyan-Khan]]. When it was his turn to be approached by the [[Lord Commander|Noyan-Khan]], Tuyo chose his Legion name to be '''Jangsai''' and he was selected to join the [[Brotherhood of the Iron Axe]].{{Fn|1a}}

After the Siege began, the White Scars suffered heavy casualties, and the Iron Axe were no exception to this. By the time [[Horus]]' forces were attacking the [[Imperial Palace]]'s inner walls, Jangsai had become the [[Space Marine Captain|Khan]] of his Brotherhood. Stationed within the Palace, Jangsai was approached by the [[Stormseer]] [[Naranbaatar]], just as its inner walls were about to fall. The Stormseer brought word that [[Ajak Khan]] of the [[Brotherhood of the Amber Eagle]] had just been killed. Naranbaatar then gave Jangsai the fallen Khan's [[Powerblade]] to wield and told him that he was being given an important mission by his [[Primarch]], [[Jaghatai Khan]].{{Fn|1a}} 

The [[Stormseer]] informed Jangsai that he was to meet with someone who came from his homeworld, [[Ar Rija]]. It was this shared background that led Jangsai to be chosen, though the [[Space Marine Captain|Khan]] was reluctant to leave and not fight at his [[Brotherhood of the Iron Axe|Brotherood]]'s side. [[Naranbaatar]] assured him, however, that he would have plenty of chances to fight soon enough. Jangsai interpreted that to mean the Siege was approaching its end, which the Stormseer confirmed to the Khan. It was for this reason, that Jangsai let go of his reluctance and asked Naranbaatar where he needed to go to begin his mission.{{Fn|1a}}

Jangsai later took part in Jaghatai Khan's counterattack to retake the [[Lion's Gate Spaceport]], surviving the battle and rallying alongside other senior remaining officers such as [[Shiban Khan]] and [[Ganzorig Noyan-Khan]] to secure the port facilities rather than fight on to the death following the wounding of the Great Khan.{{Fn|1b}} Mere hours later, Jangsai was back in battle alongside [[Ganzorig Noyan-Khan]], [[Shiban Khan]], and others to defend the retaken Lion's Gate from Traitor counterattacks.{{Fn|2}}

