Jaq Draco.wikitext:
{{InquisitionPortal}}
[[Image:JaqDraco.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Jaq Draco{{Fn|4}}]]
'''Jaq Draco''' was an [[Inquisitor]] of the [[Ordo Malleus]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
Inquisitor Jaq Draco was born on [[Xerxes Quintus]], a planet rife with [[mutant]]s and [[psyker]]s. It had only recently been rediscovered and unified within the [[Imperium]]. Draco's parents were Imperial adepts sent to the planet. After they were killed he was raised as an orphan in a [[Mission School]] on the planet. Draco was discovered to be a psyker; when a [[Black Ship]] arrived he was taken and brought to [[Terra]]. He was one of the very few aboard the Black Ship judged to be psychically powerful enough to be allowed to live and go on to become an Inquisitor.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|2a}}

===Inquisitor===
Draco and his retinue were dispatched to [[Stalinvast]] to monitor supposed [[Genestealer Cult]] activity. During their investigations, however, they were drawn to a [[Human]] [[Harlequin]] known as [[Zephro Carnelian]] and the [[Warp Entity]] known as the [[Hydra (Warp)|Hydra]]. Draco and his retinue managed to break free of the Hydra's control, but failed to capture Carnelian save his hat, which bore an image similar to the mythology of the [[Star Child]].{{Fn|1b}}

Continuing their pursuit of Carnelian, Draco enlisted the help of an [[Astropath]] known as [[Moma Parsheen]]. After briefly considering [[Exterminatus]], Draco rescinded the order after discovering that the Hydra had retreated back into the [[Warp]]. However, the order was re-issued by Moma, and Stalinvast was destroyed.{{Fn|1a}}

Continuing the hunt for Carnelian aboard his personal ship ''[[Tormentum Mallorum]]'', Draco next journeyed to a [[Space Hulk]], where he met the mysterious [[Ordo Hydra]]. Draco learned of the truth of the Ordo Hydra's mission, but upon discovering their dabbling in the Forces of [[Chaos]] condemned them as heretics.{{Fn|1c}} After discovering the Ordo Hydra extended to the highest levels of the Inquisition, Draco realised he wasn't safe and decided to travel to [[Terra]] to seek guidance from the [[Emperor]] personally.{{Fn|1d}}

Journeying to Terra by smuggling himself aboard a [[Black Ship]], Draco was guided apparently by the Emperor himself to the [[Golden Throne]]. Here, he experienced a vision in which the Emperor supposedly ordered him to destroy the Ordo Hydra. Reinvigorated, Draco and his entourage escaped Terra aboard a freighter.{{Fn|1d}}{{Fn|2b}}

===Harlequin===
[[Image:Draco Obispal Harlequin Man.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Jaq Draco, [[Harq Obispal]], and [[Zephro Carnelian]] ]]
Draco and his retinue next moved to the planet [[Luxus I]], which was revealed to him through the [[Emperor's Tarot]]. The world was in the midst of a civil war thanks to the actions of a [[Slaanesh]]i [[Chaos Cult]], and here Draco and his companions battled through [[Daemon]]s. With the help of his [[Squat]] underling [[Grimm]], Draco was able to locate the [[Navigator]] [[Azul Petrov]] and Astropath [[Fennix]] to replace those he had previously lost.{{Fn|2a}}

The group next moved to [[Darvash III]] to locate apostate director secundus of the [[Callidus Temple]], [[Tarik Ziz]] in order to undo modifications to [[Meh'Lindi]] that forced her to remain in the form of a [[Genestealer Hybrid]]. After this, Meh'Lindi was able to assume the form of an [[Eldar]] in order to infiltrate the [[Xenos]] colony via Stalinvast.{{Fn|2c}} 

At Stalinvast, the group attempted to infiltrate the Eldar but Draco discovered that his Squat underling Grimm has been secretly working for Carnelian. By interrogating Grimm, they learned that Carnelian was once [[Daemonic Possession|possessed]] by Daemons but freed by the Harlequins, who then accepted him into the ranks of the [[Illuminati]], a group dedicated to capturing the forgotten sons of the Emperor known as the [[Sensei]]. Using the Sensei, the Illuminati hoped to create a new entity that would defeat Chaos and become the new patron of Humanity.{{Fn|2d}} At Stalinvast, the group aided the Eldar against a force of [[Imperial Fists]] led by Draco's former mentor, [[Baal Firenze]]. Draco was able to escape with Carnelian's help along with [[Lexandro d'Arquebus]] and some of the remaining Imperial Fists into the [[Webway]].{{Fn|2e}}

Finding themselves on a path that may lead to the legendary [[Black Library]], the group was then stalked by a force of [[Howling Banshee]]s. During the fighting, Meh'Lindi was killed and this caused Draco to break down mentally. However, he eventually found his way into the Black Library, and discovered a book on the [[Rhana Dandra]].{{Fn|2f}}

===Chaos Child===
Driven by his grief for Meh'lindi, Draco next journeyed to [[Sabulorb]], the planet on which she had once destroyed a [[Genestealer Patriarch]]. Here they met the thief [[Rakel Binth Katzintzki]], who coveted Draco's book on the Rhana Dhandra for himself. Draco instead injected the thief with a dose of [[Polymorphine]] and psychically forced her into mimicking [[Meh'Lindi]].{{Fn|3b}} Using his new thief, Draco had her steal Eldar artefacts before the Inquisitor himself managed to kidnap a [[Death Jester]], forcing him to teach him Eldar Runes. Draco's ultimate objective was to find a point in the Webway with which to reverse time.{{Fn|3c}}

Shortly after, Draco encountered Lexandro, who had since been captured by the [[Thousand Sons]] and possessed by a [[Daemon]]. Draco was able to defeat the foe and take the Daemon into himself, but an Eldar attack forced the group to flee.{{Fn|3d}}

Draco and his entourage made for the Webway with the tent to use Rakel as a vessel to reincarnate Meh'lindi using time reversal. Upon reaching the point in the Webway in which this was possible, Rakel revealed she knew her fate but was okay with it due to the horrors she had experienced. Draco succeeded in resurrecting Meh'Lindi, but she quickly was revealed to be an insane abomination which attacked the group. Finally snapping after this failure, Draco apparently summoned a Daemon of [[Tzeentch]] into himself before being killed by Lexandro, though in truth this was just a manipulation. As he was slain in the time reversal point, Draco's soul did not enter the [[Warp]] but instead was doomed to forever roam the Webway.{{Fn|3e}}

==Retinue==
*[[Meh'lindi]] - [[Callidus Assassin]] who became the object of Draco's love and obsession. After her death in the Webway Draco became committed to resurrecting her, but the resulting abomination attacked friend and foe alike{{Fn|3e}}.
*[[Grimm]] - [[Squat]] engineer who was a secret agent of [[Zephro Carnelian]] and the [[Illuminati]]. Joins with Lexandro d'Arquebus after the death of Draco.{{Fn|3e}}
*[[Lexandro d'Arquebus]] - [[Captain]] of the [[Imperial Fists]] recruited on [[Stalinvast]]. 
*[[Moma Parsheen]] - [[Astropath]] from [[Stalinvast]]. Killed by Carnelian.{{Fn|2e}} Manipulated by Draco into killing him within the Webway.{{Fn|3e}}
*[[Rakel Binth-Kazinstzkis]] - Thief who was forced by Draco into being transformed into a "replacement" Meh'Lindi using psychic abilities and [[polymorphine]]. Eventually fled into the [[Webway]].{{Fn|3e}}
*[[Vitali Googol]] - [[Navigator]], corrupted by the [[Ordo Hydra]] and subsequently killed.{{Fn|2a}}
*[[Fennix]] - Astropath chosen to replace Parsheen. Killed by Eldar at Stalinvast.{{Fn|3d}}
*[[Azul Petrov]]  - Navigator chosen to replace Googol. Killed by Lexandro within the [[Black Library]] for attempting to steal the book of the [[Rhana Dandra]].{{Fn|2f}}

