Jemulan.wikitext:
{{WhiteScarsPortal}}
'''Jemulan''' was a member of the [[White Scars]] during the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
Jemulan was born on [[Chogoris]], however, as opposed to most of the legion, he didn't make much of his heritage as he was born in the [[Palatine (Chogoris)|Palatine's]] old domain of the [[Empty Quarter]].{{Fn|1}}

Jemulan ascended to the rank of [[Noyan-Khan]] following the death of [[Giyahun]].{{Fn|3}} He commanded the [[Horde of the Earth]].{{Fn|1a}}

During the Heresy Jemulan proved somewhat sympathetic to the Terran-born [[Warrior Lodge|Lodge]] members led by [[Hasik Noyan-Khan]] and [[Torghun Khan]] who were preaching loyalty to [[Horus]], ignoring [[Shiban Khan]]'s concerns about them.{{Fn|1a}} However when the Lodges launched their coup in the build up to the [[Second Battle of Prospero]], Jemulan sided with Shiban and led [[Keshig]] units in restoring order.{{Fn|1b}}

He had died by the fourth year of the Horus Heresy, according to the recollection of Shiban. His successor was [[Qin Fai|Qin Fai Noyan-Khan]].{{Fn|2}}

