Jeshua Thoru.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Jeshua Thoru'''{{Fn|Note 1}} was a sculptor who lived on the planet [[Verghast]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
Thoru was trained at the [[Scholam Lapidae]] in the [[hive]] city of [[Ferrozoica]]. By the time of the [[Siege of Vervunhive]], however, he lived and worked in the [[Northern Foundry Collectives]]. Amongst his works in this time period were the frieze over the portico at the Imperial Hospice in NorthCol.{{Fn|1}}

At the age of 28, in the aftermath of the [[Siege of Vervunhive]], Thoru was commissioned by Lady [[Merity Chass]] of [[House Chass]] to create an installation that would honour the [[Imperial]] victory at [[Vervunhive]], with specific aims to commemorate the hive's defenders (most notably the [[Tanith First and Only|Tanith First]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment]]) and memorialise those who died in the Siege. To this end he interviewed a number of Tanith [[Guardsmen]], including [[Colonel]] [[Colm Corbec|Corbec]], who decided to have Thoru tag along with a unit of Tanith engaged in cleanup operations in the outhabs.{{Fn|1}}

At one point in the Tanith patrol, they were fired on by enemy troops. During the resulting firefight, Thoru was able to clear a jam from [[Trooper]] [[Brostin|Brostin's]] [[flamer]], enabling him to break the deadlock that they were stuck in. Later in the fight, Thoru witnessed Trooper [[Mktag]]'s death.{{Fn|1}}

After the Imperial Guard left Verghast, Thoru returned to NorthCol and eventually completed [[Chass Memorial|his memorial to Vervunhive]], which went on to become his most celebrated work.{{Fn|1}}


