Jonah Aruken.wikitext:
{{AdeptusMechanicusPortal}}
{{ambig|subject=Moderati Primus|disambiguation=Jonah}}
'''Jonah Aruken''' was a [[Moderati|Moderati Primus]] of the [[Imperator Battle Titan]] ''[[Dies Irae]]'' during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{fn|1a}}

==Biography==
Somewhat nonchalant in his views, he enjoyed teasing his friend and fellow moderati [[Titus Cassar]] over the latter's straightedge character and adherence to the creed of the ''[[Lectitio Divinitatus]]''.{{fn|1b}} Following the [[Battle of Davin's Moon|deployment]] of the ''Dies Irae'' on [[Davin]]'s moon{{fn|1c}} and [[Horus Lupercal]]'s brush with death, Aruken and other crew of the Titan went to Cassar, looking for spiritual comfort.{{fn|1d}}

He nevertheless remained a sceptic, and his difficulty in reconciling those two sides led to frequent drinking.{{fn|2a}} Aruken's one prevailing ambition was to eventually gain command of his own Titan, a dream he felt would be jeopardized if [[Esau Turnet|Princeps Turnet]] believed he was involved with the cult.{{fn|2a}}{{fn|2c}} Still, he assisted Cassar and Kyril Sindermann when the latter sought to protect [[Euphrati Keeler]] from an assassination attempt by [[Maggard]] under Horus's orders.{{fn|2b}}

During the [[Battle of Isstvan III]], as Cassar prepared to kill Turnet, Aruken's ambition led him to kill his friend, ending the duel and allowing the ''Dies Irae'' to continue the mission given by the Warmaster — the killing of the Legions' loyalist elements.{{fn|2d}}

