Jonjon Blanchisan.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was an [[SID]] [[Robot]] programmer, and the [[Emperor]]'s personal advisor on camouflage and uniform design.{{Fn|1}}

==History==
{{PAGENAME}} was recruited to the [[Legiones Astartes]] from planet [[Stieu-Diio]] and was dismissed from initiation after destroying a consignment of Mk 14 [[Bullock]] Jetbikes in a training exercise. Jonjon was reassigned to the [[fortress-monastery]]'s maintenance facilities, where he spent years polishing chrome before being sent to program the [[SID]] [[Robots]] which apply colour, camouflage, and insignia to [[Space Marine Power Armour]].{{Fn|1}}

Blanchisan rose to prominence for his considerable talent and design philosophy: that every [[Space Marine]] is deserving of personalized iconography on all forms of their armor and equipment, as long as their unit insignia remained unobscured no restrictions need be placed on what could be portrayed.{{Fn|1}}

This philosophy lead to chief successes, allowing marines to quickly identify their battle brothers even when communications are disrupted, and helping each marine achieve identity and purpose without compromising the hierarchy necessary for a functioning chapter.{{Fn|1}}

Blanchisan's designs attracted the attention of greater forces in the imperium, including the [[Emperor of Mankind]], and now Blanchisan's SID programs are proliferated among the Space Marines of the Imperium including the commonplace forms of camouflage, such as those for jungles, ice flows, deserts, and wilderness, as well as the tremendous variety of uniform personalisations.{{Fn|1}} Blanchisan's masterwork was that of the [[Dreadnought]]s who fought in the [[Kearbea|first Battle of Kearbea]] who displayed the entirety of the chapter's battle hymn across their radiator grilles.{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was an in-universe simulacrum of [[John Blanche]].{{Fn|1}}

