Jorek the Giant.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''Jorek the Giant''' was a [[Space Wolves]] [[Space Wolves Initiate|Initiate]], who sought to conduct a [[Lone Hunt]] on a pack of [[Fenrisian Wolves]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He had tracked them to a fissure in [[Fenris]]' '''Bladed Mountains''' and watched them from the edge of a cave roof. Jorek was then about to pounce upon the [[Fenrisian Wolves|Wolves]]' alpha male, when he was suddenly attacked from behind. His targets were in fact the family of the feral [[Human]] [[Canis Wolfborn|Canis]], who had followed Jorek's tracks and struck when the [[Space Wolves Initiate|Initiate]] was about to hurt his kin. Taken by surprise, Jorek fell off the cave roof and into a circle of the wolves below. Canis then attacked again and beat Jorek unconscious, before dragging him to the [[Space Wolves]] [[Fortress Monastery|Fortress]], [[The Fang]], with the pack in tow. Once they reached it, Canis led the Fenrisian Wolves in a great howling that challenged those who would hurt his family. This was answered by [[Harald Deathwolf]], who then defeated Canis in a duel, but he was left impressed by how a mere mortal had defeated Jorek. So much so, that instead of killing Canis, Deathwolf instead inducted the feral into the Space Wolves and [[Deathwolves|his]] [[Great Company]]. However it is not known what became of Jorek afterwards.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
