Julius Gundelfo.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Julius Gundelfo''' was a '''Fourth Master Tacticae Terrestria''', amongst the hundreds of [[Imperial]] tacticae that aided the [[Primarch]] [[Dorn]]'s efforts in planning the [[Imperial Palace]]'s defenses, during the [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
Like the other tacticae, Gundelfo was considered to be amongst the [[Imperium]]'s greatest strategic thinkers, in the age of the [[Horus Heresy]]. When the [[Siege of Terra]] began, the tacticae were located in the [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Bhab Bastion]] and worked within the Bastion's '''Grand Borealis Strategium''', which served as [[Dorn]]'s main control room. They were initially safe there, as the Bastion was located in the [[Inner Palace]] and was far from the fighting. Eventually though, despite Dorn's best efforts, the forces of the traitorous [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]] reached the Inner Palace and soon began attacking the Bhab Bastion's walls.{{Fn|1}} 

Despite this, the tacticae and other [[Imperial]]s there continued their work and did not stop, even as the [[Bhab Bastion]] was invaded. It was only as the [[Traitor]]s neared the '''Grand Borealis Strategium''', that it began to be evacuated for the safety of the [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Sanctum Imperialis]]. However, this was done too late and Gundelfo was among the many Imperials who were killed within the Strategium, before they could escape.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The End and the Death: Volume I (Novel)]], 1:xvii 
