==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Huron Blackheart: Master of the Maelstrom (Novel)}}
He and his eager forces, have been charged with bringing the light of the [[Imperium]] back to the [[Galaxy]], one world at a time if need be. During the course of doing so, he was quickly approached by the [[Light of Honour]]'s [[Astropath|Chief Astropath]], [[Sethica]], who had just received{{Fn|1a}} an urgent message{{Fn|1c}}. She did not know who sent it, but believed it was a warning of an upcoming attack on an [[Imperial]] world, by a blood-red warrior bearing a black claw. Sethica then gave images associated with the world and Katra thought the message referred to{{Fn|1a}} the [[Invaders]] [[Chapter]]'s [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]] [[Ogrys‎]]{{Fn|1b}}. The blood-red warrior's identity eluded him, but Sethica had been born on [[Badab Primaris]] and believed the warrior was{{Fn|1a}} the [[Red Corsair]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]'s commander [[Huron Blackheart]].{{Fn|1b}}

With this information presented to him, Katra{{Fn|1a}} contacted the [[Ultramarines]] [[Chapter]]{{Fn|1c}} which assembled a strike force in response{{Fn|1b}}. The [[Force Captain]] and [[Sethica]]'s interpretation of the message{{Fn|1a}} was proven correct, when the strike force arrived at [[Ogrys‎]], shortly after the [[Red Corsairs]] had begun their attack upon it. The [[Chaos Warband]] was caught by surprise by the strike force's sudden invasion and retreated from Ogrys shortly afterwards{{Fn|1b}}. With that, not only was the [[Invaders]]'s [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]] saved, but the Ultramarines reclaimed the [[Battle Barge]] [[Macragge's Honour]], which had been captured by the Red Corsairs.{{Fn|1c}}

