Kadus Brekkar.wikitext:
{{DeathGuardPortal}}
'''Kadus Brekkar''' was a [[Death Guard]] [[Centurion (Rank)|Centurion]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
He was part of [[First Captain]] [[Calas Typhon]]'s [[Battle of Perditus|invasion]] of [[Perditus]], to claim the treasures the [[Mechanicus]] had discoverd there. Brekkar was sent to claim the relics at the world's '''Umbral-51''''s archaeo-vaults, with a force of [[Tactical Marine|Tactical Legionaries]], [[Grave Wardens]], [[Contemptor Dreadnought]]s and [[Mortus Poisoners]]. They were opposed, though, by the [[Iron Hands]] and later by the [[Dark Angels]], who were led by their [[Primarch]] [[Lion El'Jonson]]. When the Dark Angels arrived, El'Jonson demanded the Iron Hands and Death Guard to stand down, as they too sought the Mechanicus' relics. However both Brekkar and his Iron Hands foes refused to stop fighting to gain access to Umbral-51's vaults. The Lion sent the [[Knights Cenobium|Knight-Preceptor]] [[Vendrahel]] to claim what the vaults held, though, and his Dark Angels struck at Brekkar's. The Death Guard were overwhelmed, but further disaster struck, when Umbral's [[Tech-Priest]]s unleashed their [[Imperial Robot]]s, in order to destroy all of the invaders. This shattered Brekkar's forces and he was only able to escape further into Umbral's tunnels with squadrons of Mortus Poisoners. With any chance of successfully claiming the vaults' contents now gone, Brekkar instead sought to deny them to the Dark Angels by destroy them. Though their destruction would claim his life as well, Brekkar hoped to take many of the Dark Angels with him as well.{{Fn|1}} 

As his forces raced to the vaults, [[Vendrahel]]'s forces defeated the [[Imperial Robot]]s and raced to the vaults as well. While Brekkar reached them first, he was unable to open the gates to the vaults, before the [[Dark Angels]] reached him. The two sides were then facing each other, when the Dark Angel [[Paladin (Dark Angels)|Paladin]] [[Ennedreth]] stepped forward and challenged Brekkar to an honor duel. The [[Centurion (Rank)|Centurion]] laughed at this and instead used his [[Chem-flamer]] to reduce Ennedreth's body to ash. This enraged Vendrahel and the [[Knights Cenobium|Knight-Preceptor]] led the charge against the [[Death Guard]]. As his [[Mortus Poisoners]] then clashed with the Dark Angels, Brekkar fought Vendrahel for possession of the vaults. In the end, though, the Centurion was killed by the Knight-Preceptor and Poisoners were destroyed as well. After the battle ended, Vendrahel knelt over Brekkar's body and whispered the names of the Dark Angels who had died.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [https://www.warhammer-community.com/2022/01/17/horus-heresy-exemplary-battles-a-new-mission-and-free-rules-for-dark-angels-and-death-guard-squads/ Warhammer Community: Horus Heresy Exemplary Battles – A New Mission and Free Rules for Dark Angels and Death Guard Squads (Posted on 17/01/2022)] - [https://www.warhammer-community.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/mouvfePNquxVdprP.pdf The Battle of Perditus: Umbral-51 PDF] - pgs. 2-4 (Last accessed on 17 January 2022)

