Kaine (Captain).wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Kaine''' is a [[Mordian Iron Guard]] [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] in the [[Mordian 24th]] [[Regiment]] and he commands its [[Imperial Guard Company|Company]]'s [[Platoon|3rd Platoon]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[Image:CaptainKaine.jpg|thumb|right|220px|[[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] Kaine{{Fn|1}}]]
The [[Mordian 24th]] is among the [[Mordian Iron Guard|Iron Guard]] that are taking part in the [[Third War for Armageddon]] and and were set to counter-attack against [[Ork]] forces on the '''Sulphur River'''. However the 3rd was left behind, as their [[Chimera]]s were taken by the Company so it could be fully mobile for the counter-attack. Instead, the [[Platoon]] was charged with guarding the [[Regiment]]'s supplies, within a ruined mine that was close to the Sulphur River's '''Asch Creek''', until the 24th returned. Unfortunately disaster struck soon afterwards, when the Regiment was almost completely destroyed by an [[Ork]] ambush and its few survivors were unable to warn Kaine about their defeat. An Ork [[Warboss]] then led a horde against the unsuspecting Platoon, along with the Hive Militia, civilians and the [[Ratling Sniper]] [[Hookey (Mordian Iron Guard)|Hookey]], the 24th left behind as well. Though vastly outnumbered, the 3rd is unaware that the Orks only have a limited time to battle the Platoon, before the horde has to return to the Xenos' main camp.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
*The [[Mordian 24th]] were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Jervis Johnson]]. They were featured in [[Citadel Journal 48]].{{Fn|1}}
*The ''Last Stand at Asch Creek'' is a modified version of the [[Battle of Glazer's River]] scenario, which appeared in [[White Dwarf 222 (UK)]]. Besides the change in [[Regiment]] and location, the [[Platoon]] is led by [[Kaine (Captain)|Kaine]], instead of [[Caine (Captain)|Caine]]. The names of the characters Hookey and Blikk, however, remain the same.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Citadel Journal 48]], pgs. 20-24 — ''Last Stand at Asch Creek''

