Kalae Korvydae.wikitext:
{{RavenGuardPortal}}
[[Image:Korvydae-mini.jpg|thumb|right|Shadow Captain Korvydae{{Fn|2}}]]
'''Kalae Korvydae''' is the current [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Raven Guard]] [[Chapter|Chapter's]] [[10th Company (Raven Guard)|10th Company]].{{Fn|1}} 

==Overview==
Korvydae is seen as a fearsome opponent in combat, exemplifying his Chapter’s mastery of hit and run tactics.{{Fn|2}}  He also serves as the Raven Guard's [[Master of Recruits]] and overseer of the training of the [[Space Marine Scout]]s.  However, Korvydae himself prefers to delegate much of the actual training to his subordinate [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]]s in preference for leading his men into battle.{{Fn|3}}

Korvydae was recently absent from his position within the chapter; having planned and lead the ill-fated [[Raid on Kastorel-Novem]] in [[992.M41]], Korvydae volunteered for two years of service in the [[Deathwatch]] to atone for his failures.{{Fn|3}}

==Tactics==
Korvydae is a master of raiding and sabotage tactics, preferring to field a fast-moving assault force, giving prominence to [[Assault Squad]]s in his plans for capturing and holding objectives.{{Fn|3}}

He leads his Scouts in long range recon and sabotage missions, relaying reports to other units which can then enact the lightning hit-and-run raids that the Raven Guard are famous for.{{Fn|3}}

In comparison to his contemporary captains such as [[Kayvaan Shrike]], it is noted that very few outside of the chapter have ever heard of Korvydae.  This is agreeable to Korvydae as he prefers the anonymity of leading his stealth or lightning strike raids where his work can remain unseen.{{Fn|3}}

==Equipment==
Korvydae equips himself with a [[Jump Pack]], [[Bolt Pistol]], [[Artificer Armour]] and a [[Thunder Hammer]] drawn from the chapter armoury as well the [[Iron Halo]] as befits his rank.{{Fn|3}}

