Kardozia.wikitext:
{{IronHandsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Space Marine Dreadnought|Dreadnought]] [[Iron Father]] in the [[Iron Hands]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
[[Image:Kardozia.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Kardozia{{Fn|2}}]]
Kardozia was not with his Legion when they were decimated during the [[Dropsite Massacre]]. When he learned of what had befallen the Iron Hands, and his [[Primarch]] [[Ferrus Manus]]' death, Kardozia took his [[Cruiser|Patrol Cruiser]] ''[[Light of Battle]]'', as well as the three squads he had under his command, and began targeting the supply convoys of [[Horus]]' forces and any warships they would be able to destroy.{{Fn|1}}

He would continue do this until the later years of the civil war, when he learned that Horus' forces where massing in the [[Beta-Garmon System]], which led directly into the [[Segmentum Solar]] and [[Terra]] itself. The Imperium's loyal forces were moving to stop the Traitors however, and the embattled system became one of [[Battle of Beta-Garmon|the largest battles]] in the Heresy's history. Kardozia decided he needed to aid the Imperium's forces there and took the ''Light of Battle'' into the [[Warp]]. However, while traveling through the Warp, the [[Psyker|psychic]] Iron Hand [[Dalves]], who served under his command, made psychic contact with the [[Raven Guard]] Legion's [[Chief Librarian]], [[Balsar Kurthuri]], who was also traveling through the Warp with his Primarch [[Corax]] aboard their flagship, the [[Battle Barge]] ''[[Avenger (Battle Barge)|Avenger]]''. Once he learned of this Kardozia asked to arrange a meeting with Corax, as the Iron Father wanted to exchange information on what was occurring in the civil war and, more importantly, hopefully convince the Raven Guard to join him in fighting in the Beta-Garmon System. Though the two leaders would meet aboard the ''Avenger'', they could not agree on what to do after Kardozia informed Corax of the battle in Beta-Garmon. Corax stated that it would a wasted effort to join what he thought was already a lost battle, as with Horus personally leading the forces there, he had no doubt the Traitors' victory was assured. Kardozia made the point that, even if they were doomed to lose in Beta-Garmon, the Imperium's forces had to make Horus pay in blood and armour for his victory and for every step the [[Warmaster]] took towards Terra. Eventually though, it was clear neither could change the other's mind and they bid each other farewell.{{Fn|1}}

Once aboard the ''Light of Battle'', Kardozia was true to his word and headed directly for the Beta-Garmon System. His fate after that is unknown.{{Fn|1}}

