'''{{PAGENAME}}''' ([[rosette]] number 7134/S3{{fn|13a}}) is a [[Radical]]{{Fn|11}} (though she was initially a [[Puritan]]) [[Inquisitor]] of the [[Ordo Hereticus]].{{Fn|1}}

===Biography===
Greyfax was imprisoned within a [[Tesseract Vault]] by the [[Necron Overlord]] [[Trazyn|Trazyn the Infinite]] for centuries until she was released, along with his other prisoners, to aid the [[Imperium|Imperium's]] forces on [[Cadia]] during the [[13th Black Crusade]]. Despite being a powerful [[Psyker]] herself, when Greyfax emerged she was shocked at the sight of [[Sanctioned Psyker|Imperial psyker]]s using their powers without sanction and to see the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter|Chapter's]] [[Wulfen]] running rampant on the battlefield. What left her utterly appalled, though, was seeing how the Imperial defenders of Cadia worshiped the so-called [[Living Saint]], [[Celestine]], as it was nothing short of idolatry in Greyfax's mind. These sights, however, have not shaken her unwavering faith in the [[Emperor of Mankind|Emperor]] and Greyfax is committed to aiding the Imperium in defending Cadia. Greyfax ultimately worked alongside these psychic abominations and mutants in battling [[Ezekyle Abaddon|Abaddon]] personally.{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}

Ultimately, however, Cadia fell and Greyfax fled to the outer system with several of her allies, such as [[Saint Celestine]] and [[Belisarius Cawl]]. Hounded by the [[Black Legion]], they were guided into the [[Webway]] on [[Kalisus]] by [[Eldrad Ulthran]].{{Fn|2}}

Greyfax accompanied Celestine during the subsequent [[Ultramar Campaign]] and fought in the [[Fortress of Hera]] as [[Roboute Guilliman]] was reborn. She took part in the resulting [[Terran Crusade]] and was one of the few of the Imperial expedition to reach Terra. During the voyage she finally put her suspicion toward unnatural entities like Celestine past her, and was freed from Trazyn's [[Mindshackle Scarab]] by Belisarius Cawl. Once on [[Terra]], Celestine and Greyfax announced their intent to spread their blessings across Terra and report to their masters in the Ordo Hereticus.{{Fn|3}}

Later, Inquisitors Greyfax and [[Thadus Valconet Horst|Horst]] and a squad of [[Grey Knights]] were sent by [[Roboute Guilliman]] to recover the [[Eye of Night]]. The two inquisitors entered the [[Eye of Terror]], seeking the location of the Eye of Night from [[Moriana]], who revealed that Horst knew the location but that he was suffering from amnesia. She gave them a [[daemon]]ic guide who led them to a [[daemon prince]] who held Horst's body and the Eye of Night. Greyfax killed the daemon (and Horst in the process), recovering the Eye of Night from within its body.{{Fn|4}}

Greyfax has been active in combating the enemies of mankind since her return, such as working with the [[White Scars]] to set a trap of [[Deathstrike Missile Launcher]]s that obliterated the [[Death Guard]] on the world of [[Dortwyr]].{{Fn|5}} The Inquisitor has found recent prominence due to her fanatical purges of [[Necron]] forces localized around [[Ultramar]].{{Fn|6}}

She later became embroiled in the affairs of [[Ecclesiarch]] [[Decius XXIII]], who was attempting to repeal the [[Decree Passive]]. She saved the Ecclesiarch from several assassination attempts alongside [[Saint Celestine]]. The two servants of the [[Emperor]] bonded during the journey to [[Ophelia VII]] to protect the Ecclesiarch. In the end, it was revealed the entire affair was a plan by the [[Tyrant of Blueflame]] to manifest into the Materium by taking Celestine's body. After the Tyrant was defeated, the two parted ways.{{Fn|8}}

By the several year mark of the [[Indomitus Crusade]], Greyfax had taken control of the Inquisitorial Conclave based on [[Luna]] and oversaw the fortress there. She spoke to her subordinate [[Rostov]] on the matter of the [[Hand of Abaddon]] seeking to reconstruct the [[Anathame]].{{Fn|10}}

At some point, Inquisitor Greyfax executed the Ordo Xenos Inquisitor [[Helynna Valeria]], who, like Greyfax, was once discovered to be under the influence of Trazyn's [[Mindshackle Scarab]]s.{{Fn|9}}

Later, having learned of the many and varied threats to the [[Imperium]], she adopted the [[Radical]] mindset. In the "new" galaxy, all means are good - as long as they serve the good of Humanity itself.{{Fn|11}}

===Weapon and Equipment===
{{PAGENAME}} is armed with a master-crafted [[power sword]], a master-crafted [[condemnor boltgun]], and a [[psyocculum]] – the ''Eye of the Emperor''.{{Fn|7}}

