Ke.wikitext:
{{TauPortal}}
'''[[Fio'ui]] [[Tau'n]] Ke''', simply known as '''Ke''', is an [[Earth Caste]] [[Engineer]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
Ke was deployed for the war for [[Cao Quo]] and its moon [[Thapes Quo]] against the [[Imperium]] where she was responsible for helping erect a communications amplifier at Castellum Epiphania.{{Fn|1a}} They are attacked by human rebels, and Ke is rescued by a squad of [[Fire Warrior]]s led by [[Swordlight]] and the [[Water Caste]] operative [[Orr]].{{Fn|1b}}  Ke and the others evacuate back to Thapes Quo Operating base, where the [[Ethereal]] [[Aun'ui Yor'i]] reveals that to rescue the missing Ethereal [[Aun'ui Kir'qath]], an [[Elemental Council]] would be formed with Ke, Swordlight, Orr, [[Sei]], and the Human [[Gue'vesa]] agent [[Jules Rare]].{{Fn|1c}}

During their subsequent mission, Ke grows close to most of the squad as they unravel a conspiracy involving the mysterious [[Syra]] group that spreads to the highest levels of Tau command which the rescued Kir'qath had discovered. In the final battle at the Cao Quo floating forward operating base, Orr is killed by a Imperial [[Callidus Assassin]] who is revealed to have been impersonating Yor'i{{Fn|1d}} while Ke and Swordlight battle the [[Raptors (Chapter)|Raptors]] [[Sergeant]] [[Artamax]]. Ke is able to interfere with Artamax's armour interface, allowing Swordlight to slash his throat and kill the Marine. Ke and Swordlight, alongside the [[Kroot]] [[Ghodh]], are then able to corner and wound the Imperial assassin.{{Fn|1e}}

Ultimately, Ke survives the mission on Cao Quo alongside Swordlight and meets with the real Yor'i, who commends them for their work but notes that to spare the Human population of Cao Quo future violence that he had ordered a withdrawal from the planet.{{Fn|1f}}

