Keorn Asata.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
[[Image:KeornAsata.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Keorn Asata{{Fn|1c}}]]

{{QuoteBox|quote='''"These new recruits don't seem to have the right stuff. Dammit, when I first arrived here I didn't even get the privilege of the Ambull hunt." - Captain Keorn Asata'''{{Fn|1a}}}}
'''Keorn Asata''' was [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|2nd Company]] and the Chapter's [[Master of Ordnance]] in late [[M41]].{{Fn|1b}}

==History==
Asata was born around 937.[[M41]] on a [[Hive World]]. By age thirteen he had joined a [[gang|street gang]], and was captured that year (950.M41) during an [[Ultramarines]] [[Ultramarines#Recruitment|recruiting mission]]. He underwent tissue compatibility and psychology tests and was earmarked for partial cerebral reprogramming. Though this was successful, it did not remove his "rough edge", and he remained a ruthless warrior with a naturally alert temperament and rather brash manner.{{Fn|1c}}

Asata was stationed to a fortress, and was initiated into the [[Ultramarines]] in battle with the [[Tyranids]], which he was injured and permanently scarred from. He was taken back to the [[Apothecarion]] and healed, but as soon as he was out of the Apothecarion he was made to go on an [[Ambull]] hunt.{{Fn|1a}}

He became a [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], and while at the fortress got to know half-[[Eldar]], half-[[Human]] [[Chief Librarian]] and [[Astropath]] [[Illiyan Nastase]]. He was highly suspicious of [[psykers]], and was always unnerved by Nastase, who he regarded with more than a little trepidation.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1c}}

[[Image:KeornAsataBadge.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Keorn Asata's Badge{{Fn|1d}}]]
In 985.[[M41]], the Ultramarines lost many [[Dreadnoughts]] during a skirmish against [[Ork]]s on [[Burbeck's Asteroid]]. Asata wanted to see [[Master of the Forge]] [[Samuel Dexter]] replace the lost Dreadnoughts, instead of carrying out his [[Robot]]ic research, which caused friction between the two for some years.{{Fn|1b}}

By 987.[[M41]], Asata was the Chapter's [[Master of Ordnance]] as well as Captain of [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|2nd Company]], aided by [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] [[Dieta]], and [[Chaplain]] [[Maginty]]. He was the only Ultramarines [[Master (Space Marine)|Master]] who also led the Captaincy of a [[Space Marine Company|Company]] at that time.{{Fn|1b}}

During an [[Ambull]] hunt to test new Ultramarines recruits, Asata climbed the winding steps of the fortress to the uppermost battlements, and found [[Chief Librarian]] [[Illiyan Nastase|Nastase]] there. He considered killing the half-[[Eldar]] [[psyker]], but spat venomously instead, and asked him if he had detected the recruits. He was disdainful when he heard that the new recruits seemed to have taken more casualties than expected, and recounted the story of his initiation to Nastase, which he had told him many times before.{{Fn|1a}}

==Equipment==
As the [[Ultramarines]] [[Master of Ordnance]], Asata was entitled to wear a scarlet ceremonial floor-length cloak, with a unique badge woven in gold onto the cloak's collar.{{Fn|1b}}

Asata wore [[Mark VI]] [[Power Armour]] with the [[Master of Ordnance]] badge on his shoulder pad, and a [[refractor field]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}

He carried an intricately inlaid [[power sword]], as well as a [[boltgun]], [[bolt pistol]], and a [[Astartes Combat Knife|knife]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1c}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
===Conflicting sources===
Later editions have an entirely different set of [[Space Marine Captain|Captains]] of the [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|2nd Company]], with [[Severus Agemman]] as Captain until the [[Battle for Macragge]] in 745.[[M41]], followed by [[Cato Sicarius]] until early in the [[Indomitus Crusade]], when he was lost to the [[Warp]] and was succeeded by [[Sevastus Acheran]].{{Fn|2}}{{Fn|3}}

