Kerenna.wikitext:
{{AdeptaSororitasPortal}}
'''Kerenna''' was a [[Adepta Sororitas|Sister]] of the [[Order of Our Martyred Lady]] and was among its forces that served in [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus]]'s [[Battle Group Jovia]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
She always had an eye for the ebb and flow of battle and used it during her service in [[Battle Group Jovia|Jovia]]. This ability was noted by [[Canoness]] [[Felicita]], who claimed that Kerenna could one day succeed her because of it. They both served in the Battle Group's '''Task Force IX''', when it was sent to reclaim the [[Imperium Sanctus]] world [[Garvetha Primus]] and its [[system]] from [[Heretics]]. The Task Force invaded the world and soon only needed to conquer the city of '''Deng-Var''', to make Garvetha Primus' the [[Imperium]]'s once more. This would then allow the world's system to be opened up for further invasions. However it was as they were fighting to take back the city, that the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Angron]] destroyed the [[Choral Engine]] on the [[Imperium Nihilus]] world [[Malakbael]], which the majority of [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus|Fleet Quartus]]' forces had been defending. The [[psychic]] beacon's subsequent explosion, then unleashed [[Khorne]]'s [[Murder-Curse]] [[Warp]] plague, within Malakbael's [[Malak System|system]]. However due to its Battle Groups sharing psychic channels with each other, the Murder-Curse was able to spread to them all, no matter where they were located within the [[Galaxy]].{{Fn|1}}  

Because of this, the [[Warp]] plague soon reached '''Task Force IX''' and those who were infected by it, immediately became servants of the [[Khorne|Blood God]]. Now filled with murderous bloodlust and rage, they then fell upon anyone that was near them, including their former allies. While [[Canoness]] [[Felicita]] was infected by the [[Murder-Curse]], Kerenna was able to resist it, but she felt this was done by sheer will power alone. If her will broke, Kerenna knew she would join the Canoness in damnation. Her fellow [[Adepta Sororitas]] Sister, [[Helenica]] also managed to avoid the plague, but was suddenly decapitated near Kerenna, by an infected [[Repentia]]. The traitor met her end at Kerenna's hands seconds later and she believed the [[Emperor]] Himself intervened to make sure she did not fall to the Murder-Curse. Kerenna thought it was because of her observation ability, that allowed her to see a pattern within the infected's behavior. In her observations, the more lucid of the plague's victims could form packs of infected, that follow their commands. If given enough time, Kerenna thought these packs would be able to merge into a hellish army of corrupted souls. Certain that she was the only [[Imperial]] on [[Garvetha Primus]] who had made this observation, Kerenna knew this was why Emperor had spared her. She then sought to tell other non-infected Imperials of what she had discovered, but Kerenna was killed mere moments later, by the corrupted crew of the Task Force [[Warhound]], [[Venatoris Brutalor]].{{Fn|1}}  

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Arks of Omen: Angron]], pgs. 46-49 

