'''Kessel''' is an [[Inquisitor]] and ex-[[Daemonhost]] once possessed by the [[Daemon]] [[Loa Gorg]] who now unwillingly serves him.{{Fn|1}}

==Overview==
A part of Loa Gorg's essence remained within Kessel and forced the Daemon to cooperate with the Inquisitor, since his death would result in the release this soul-fragment and the destruction of the Daemon. This state of affairs lasted for three decades, the daemonic presence corrupting Kessel more and more. This would eventually have killed Kessel but he finally managed to transfer the soul-fragment into a [[Daemonsword]] that the Inquisitor now wields. This weapon extend his life as long as he is in possession of it, and he has been purging the unclean and researching [[Chaos]] for nearly two centuries.{{Fn|3}}

He has frequently crossed paths with the fellow Inquisitors [[Tyrus]] and [[Lichtenstein]], each vying for him for their own ends.  After Lichtenstein saved Kessel from Tyrus' prison at [[Cephalon]] Spaceport, the Daemonhost granted Lichtenstein safe passage to [[Equinox]].{{Fn|1}} 

Kessel is a dedicated member of the  [[Chaoticians]], precursors to the [[Xanthism|Xanthite movement]], and was drawn to the world of [[Karis Cephalon]] looking for the device called [[the Angel]]. This lead to a conflict with Inquisitor Lichtenstein that was also looking for the Angel.{{Fn|3}}

==Retinue==
*[[Loa Gorg]] - [[Daemonhost]], part of its essence is trapped in Kessel's [[Daemonsword]].{{Fn|3}}
*[[Mechsimus Oilreliu]] - [[chrono-gladiator]] whose inbuilt chronometer was halted by Kessel after Mechsimus saved the former's life from a [[Siddith Assassin]].
*[[Logan Storm]] - ex-[[skitarii]], from the [[Forge World]] [[Transix Seven]].{{Fn|3}}{{Fn|4}}

